('112.4.b.12.B',2,'What is a PRODUCER in a food chain?','["a living thing that makes its own food", "the Moon", "an animal that eats other animals", "a rock"]'::jsonb,0,'Plants are producers that make their own food.','original'),
('112.4.b.12.B',2,'What is a CONSUMER?','["a cloud", "a living thing that eats other living things", "a plant that makes food from sunlight", "a rock"]'::jsonb,1,'Consumers cannot make their own food, so they eat other living things.','original'),
('112.4.b.12.B',3,'In the food chain grass → rabbit → fox, which kind of living thing is the producer?','["an animal that eats meat", "a rock", "a plant", "an animal that eats plants"]'::jsonb,2,'Grass is a plant, and plants make their own food from sunlight.','original'),
('112.4.b.12.B',3,'Algae are tiny plant-like living things in water. A small fish eats the algae. What does the small fish get from eating them?','["sand", "shells", "bubbles", "energy"]'::jsonb,3,'Animals get energy from the food they eat.','original'),
('112.4.b.12.B',3,'A caterpillar eats leaves. A bird eats the caterpillar. Which is a consumer?','["the caterpillar and the bird", "only the leaves", "none of them", "the leaves and the bird"]'::jsonb,0,'Both animals are consumers.','original'),
('112.4.b.12.B',2,'Which animal eats ONLY plants?','["a shark", "a rabbit", "a hawk", "a lion"]'::jsonb,1,'A rabbit eats plants only.','original'),
